rsible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["6 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm (with a citation to the client's retry contract, or an added assertion) that MCPRetiringError is surfaced as a retryable status the streamable-HTTP client re-routes to green — or state explicitly that client retry is an existing, verified contract out of scope.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a certified request arriving mid-drain is rejected so the client retries the live (green) container and the gauge can actually reach 0'","Fix 1 tests assert refusal + no-increment only; no assertion about client retry semantics"],"finding":"The load-bearing claim that a refused certified op causes the client to 'retry the live (green) container' (so the retiring gauge can actually reach 0) has no proving step. The tests verify only that MCPRetiringError is raised and the gauge is not incremented on the server side; nothing verifies the client treats MCPRetiringError as a retryable, re-route-to-green signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f929979bc55d3a2b3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Fix 1, third bullet ('the client retries the live (green) container'); Testing → Fix 1","norm_id":"n4804a89418a8bb73","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the MCP client surfaces MCPRetiringError as a hard failure instead of retrying, the intake-refusal converts a silent wait into a visible client-facing error during every rollout."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Cite the existing client retry handling for MCPRetiringError (status code / error class) in the plan, or add an AC asserting the error is emitted with the retryable status the client already honors.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a concrete default value (in seconds) for DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS in the plan, with a one-line rationale for why it is safe as an idle-stream backstop.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6114,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add a short constant `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS`'","'sweeps idle held-open streams in seconds instead of the full 1200s'","AC asserts only 'timeout_graceful_shutdown == DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS' and '< DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS'"],"finding":"The new constant DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS is described only as 'a short constant' / 'short backstop' with no concrete value; the AC only requires it be `< DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` (1200), leaving the actual number an unstated decision for the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7e03aea73ec8c1f7","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Fix 1, first bullet; AC line 1","norm_id":"n91f61dcd74584736","priority":0.1886,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks an arbitrary short value that is too aggressive (force-closes a stream mid-write) or too slow (port still pinned longer than intended)."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Name a specific value (e.g. DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS = 10) and note that the real op bound is enforced by the gauge poll, so the backstop only needs to sweep idle held-open streams.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the draining-check and the gauge increment are performed atomically (single lock/CAS) so a certified op cannot pass the not-draining check and increment after begin_draining()/the drain loop observes 0, and add a concurrency test for that race.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8263,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'REFUSE a new certified op (raise MCPRetiringError, never incrementing) once draining'","Plan: '_on_sigterm calls begin_draining() FIRST (immediate intake-stop), before the drain loop'","T9 TOCTOU clause: shared/mutable state must be mutated atomically (no check-then-act) even when lifecycle is fully specified"],"finding":"The new `draining` flag on InFlightGauge creates a check-then-act sequence with the increment: the certified-op wrapper checks `draining` and, if not draining, increments the gauge. The plan does not specify that the draining-check and the increment are atomic relative to `begin_draining()`. A certified request could pass the not-draining check concurrently with `begin_draining()` firing, then increment after the drain loop has already observed 0 in-flight — re-pinning the port the fix is meant to free, or racing the should_exit flip.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe04ff02718712f7f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, Fix 1 — 'add a draining flag to InFlightGauge (begin_draining()), and have the certified-op wrapper REFUSE a new certified op ... once draining'","norm_id":"n97ebe75b7abcaa14","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Under concurrent SIGTERM + inbound certified request, the draining check races the increment; request increments after drain loop reads 0, so the retiring container stays busy/pinned or an in-flight op is force-closed by the short uvicorn backstop"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Guard the draining-flag read and the increment under the gauge's existing lock (or an atomic CAS), and add a test that fires begin_draining() interleaved with an increment attempt to assert the increment is refused.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the rollback (redeploy prior release) and confirm old (should_exit-first) + new (refuse-first) MCP containers coexisting during the rollout window is benign.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'This replaces uvicorn's should_exit-first intake-stop ... with an explicit refusal'","Plan states fixes are 'reversible' but names no concrete undo step; no explicit rollback line in Acceptance Criteria","T12 anti-FP: internal-only change with trivial revert is fine — but coexistence of old+new during rollout should be confirmed benign"],"finding":"The plan does not state an explicit rollback path for the shutdown-intake semantics change. Fix 1 replaces uvicorn's should_exit-first intake-stop with an explicit refusal, changing how retiring containers behave during a rolling deploy where old (should_exit-first) and new (refuse-first) containers coexist. While trivially revertible by redeploying the prior release, the plan should state that as the rollback and note the old/new coexistence is benign.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbdea91e2924073c5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, Fix 1 / Scope","norm_id":"nb56c61769f56d844","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["During the deploy that lands this fix, a client mid-retirement may hit an old container (waits full grace) and a new container (refuses+retries green) in the same window; plan should confirm this mixed behavior is safe and name redeploy-prior-release as the rollback"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","rever